{
  "meta": {
    "id": "hielo-flota-en",
    "lang": "en",
    "title": "Why ice floats",
    "fps": 30,
    "width": 1080,
    "height": 1920,
    "voice": {
      "engine": "chatterbox",
      "voice": "default",
      "speed": 1.0
    },
    "music": false,
    "captionEmphasis": "box"
  },
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "b01",
      "role": "hook",
      "text": "Have you ever wondered why ice floats, if it's just solid water?",
      "keyword": "floats,",
      "scene": {
        "env": "interior_neutro",
        "light": "noche",
        "hero": {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "asset": "vaso_agua_hielo",
          "pose": "centro"
        },
        "camera": {
          "preset": "push_in",
          "rate": 0.2
        },
        "dof": 14
      },
      "overlays": [
        {
          "type": "PulseRings",
          "at": "floats,",
          "anchor": "hero",
          "color": "ui.cyan"
        }
      ],
      "transition": "glide",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "pulse",
          "at": "ice"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b02",
      "role": "tension",
      "text": "Almost every substance shrinks when it freezes, and its solid form sinks. Water does exactly the opposite, and that changes everything.",
      "keyword": "opposite,",
      "scene": {
        "env": "interior_neutro",
        "light": "noche",
        "hero": {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "asset": "vaso_agua_hielo",
          "pose": "lateral"
        },
        "camera": {
          "preset": "orbit_slow",
          "deg": 45
        },
        "dof": 12
      },
      "overlays": [
        {
          "type": "Pill",
          "at": "sinks.",
          "text": "IT SINKS",
          "color": "ui.red"
        }
      ],
      "transition": "zoom_through",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "spin",
          "at": "opposite",
          "dur": 40
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b03",
      "role": "mechanism",
      "text": "When water freezes, it expands by about nine percent. That's why a full bottle of water can burst in the freezer.",
      "keyword": "expands",
      "scene": {
        "env": "tech_oscuro",
        "light": "tech",
        "hero": {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "asset": "moleculas_agua",
          "pose": "red_hexagonal"
        },
        "camera": {
          "preset": "orbit_slow",
          "deg": 12
        },
        "dof": 8
      },
      "overlays": [
        {
          "type": "StatCallout",
          "at": "nine",
          "value": 9,
          "suffix": " %",
          "label": "MORE VOLUME WHEN FROZEN",
          "color": "warm.gold"
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Properties_of_water",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice"
      ],
      "transition": "glide",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scale",
          "at": "expands",
          "to": 1.25,
          "dur": 40
        },
        {
          "type": "burst",
          "at": "burst",
          "anchor": "top"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b04",
      "role": "mechanism",
      "text": "Blame the molecules. In ice, they lock into hexagons that leave gaps inside. A liter of ice weighs about nine hundred seventeen grams, and a liter of water, a thousand.",
      "keyword": "hexagons",
      "scene": {
        "env": "tech_oscuro",
        "light": "tech",
        "hero": {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "asset": "moleculas_agua",
          "pose": "red_hexagonal"
        },
        "camera": {
          "preset": "push_in",
          "rate": 0.25
        },
        "dof": 10
      },
      "overlays": [
        {
          "type": "BarCompare",
          "at": "liter",
          "unit": "g per liter",
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Ice",
              "value": 917,
              "color": "ui.cyan"
            },
            {
              "label": "Water",
              "value": 1000,
              "color": "warm.gold"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice",
        "https://www.britannica.com/science/ice"
      ],
      "transition": "crossfade",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "halo",
          "at": "gaps",
          "color": "ui.cyan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b05",
      "role": "layer2",
      "text": "And here's where it gets interesting. Liquid water is densest at about four degrees, so that water sinks to the bottom of lakes.",
      "keyword": "four",
      "scene": {
        "env": "interior_neutro",
        "light": "dorado",
        "hero": {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "asset": "lago_corte",
          "pose": "corte"
        },
        "camera": {
          "preset": "glide"
        },
        "dof": 6
      },
      "overlays": [
        {
          "type": "StatCallout",
          "at": "four",
          "value": 4,
          "suffix": " °C",
          "label": "DENSEST WATER",
          "color": "ui.cyan"
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Properties_of_water"
      ],
      "transition": "cut",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "arrow",
          "at": "bottom",
          "anchor": "fondo",
          "dir": "down"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b06",
      "role": "twist",
      "text": "That's why lakes freeze from the top down. Ice doesn't bury life: it protects it, like a lid against the cold.",
      "keyword": "protects",
      "scene": {
        "env": "interior_neutro",
        "light": "atardecer",
        "hero": {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "asset": "lago_corte",
          "pose": "corte"
        },
        "camera": {
          "preset": "drift",
          "dir": "left"
        },
        "dof": 12
      },
      "overlays": [
        {
          "type": "Callout3D",
          "at": "lid",
          "anchor": "top",
          "text": "Ice: insulator"
        }
      ],
      "transition": "crossfade",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "halo",
          "at": "protects",
          "anchor": "hielo",
          "color": "ui.cyan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b07",
      "role": "cta",
      "text": "What other weird thing about water should I explain next? Tell me in the comments below.",
      "keyword": "comments",
      "scene": {
        "env": "interior_neutro",
        "light": "noche",
        "hero": {
          "kind": "primitive",
          "asset": "vaso_agua_hielo",
          "pose": "centro"
        },
        "camera": {
          "preset": "zoom_through"
        },
        "dof": 14
      },
      "overlays": [],
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ]
}
